response:
24.35 Should differences in government legislation and funding models between countries be taken into account when planning education and training for students in countries where quality education in science is limited or is provided by the government at a relatively low level?
Yes; Yes; No; No; No;
A well established model for learning such as Socratic inquiry, inquiry learning, collaborative learning and the flipped classroom can be used effectively in any learning environment. These methods can be especially important when trying to foster the abilities of a largely illiterate and under educated population where resources are limited.
